#: angular/README.md
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"A standalone Angular app (via Vite + `@analogjs/vite-plugin-angular`, no "
"Angular CLI) styled with\n"
"[`@pantoken/components`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/components) "
"and\n"
"[`@pantoken/angular`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/angular) "
"(pantoken custom elements\n"
"for Angular).\n"
"\n"
"## Develop\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## What's here\n"
"\n"
"- `src/main.ts` calls `registerPantokenElements()` (from `@pantoken/"
"angular`) once at bootstrap so\n"
"  elements like `<instui-icon>` work in templates, and imports the token/"
"component CSS plus\n"
"  `@pantoken/interactions` (wires up modal, tooltip, and other component "
"behaviors out of the\n"
"  box).\n"
"- `src/app.component.ts` is a standalone component (`CUSTOM_ELEMENTS_SCHEMA` "
"lets the template\n"
"  compiler accept pantoken's custom element tags) whose template is styled "
"with `instui-*`\n"
"  classes; optional insertion points (header, filters, content, trailing) "
"are marked with\n"
"  `<div data-slot=\"...\">`.\n"
"- Apply classes like `class=\"instui-button\"` to markup; see the\n"
"  [component reference](https://pantoken.app/api/css) for the full class "
"list.\n"
"\n"
"## Learn more\n"
"\n"
"See the [getting started guide](https://pantoken.app/guide/getting-started) "
"to learn more.\n"
msgstr ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"En frittstående Angular-app (via Vite + `@analogjs/vite-plugin-angular`, "
"ingen Angular CLI) stylet med\n"
"[`@pantoken/components`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/components) "
"og\n"
"[`@pantoken/angular`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/angular) "
"(pantoken tilpassede elementer\n"
"for Angular).\n"
"\n"
"## Utvikle\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Hva som er her\n"
"\n"
"- `src/main.ts` kaller `registerPantokenElements()` (fra `@pantoken/"
"angular`) én gang ved bootstrap slik at\n"
"  elementer som `<instui-icon>` fungerer i templater, og importerer token-/"
"komponent-CSS pluss\n"
"  `@pantoken/interactions` (kobler opp modal, tooltip og andre "
"komponentatferder ferdig).\n"
"- `src/app.component.ts` er en frittstående komponent "
"(`CUSTOM_ELEMENTS_SCHEMA` lar template-\n"
"  kompilatoren akseptere pantokens tilpassede elementtagger) hvis template "
"er stylet med `instui-*`\n"
"  klasser; valgfrie innsettingspunkter (header, filters, content, trailing) "
"er markert med\n"
"  `<div data-slot=\"...\">`.\n"
"- Bruk klasser som `class=\"instui-button\"` på markup; se\n"
"  [komponentreferansen](https://pantoken.app/api/css) for full "
"klasseoversikt.\n"
"\n"
"## Lær mer\n"
"\n"
"Se [kom i gang-guiden](https://pantoken.app/guide/getting-started) for mer "
"informasjon.\n"

#: canvas-theme-editor/README.md
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"Upload-ready assets for Canvas LMS's **Theme Editor**, plus a local preview "
"for authoring Rich\n"
"Content Editor (RCE) page templates styled with\n"
"[`@pantoken/components`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"components).\n"
"\n"
"## What's here\n"
"\n"
"- `theme.css` / `theme.js` — upload these two files under **Theme Editor → "
"Advanced** in Canvas.\n"
"  They're built for the CDN provider/theme/mode you chose when scaffolding "
"(`--cdn`/`--theme`/\n"
"  `--theme-mode`; jsDelivr/rebrand/light by default) and include a loader "
"for\n"
"  `@pantoken/interactions` (wires up component behaviors like modal, "
"tooltip, and drilldown).\n"
"- `index.html` / `src/main.ts` — a local, TinyMCE-based editor (`npm run "
"dev`) that mirrors Canvas's\n"
"  RCE so you can author page templates against pantoken's classes before "
"copying them into Canvas.\n"
"  The page itself is built with pantoken's `wrapper` layout: click **Edit "
"theme** to open a tray\n"
"  with **Config** / **CSS** / **JS** tabs (CDN provider/theme/mode selects, "
"and syntax-highlighted,\n"
"  hand-editable copies of `theme.css`/`theme.js` that feed the live "
"preview), and the **?** button\n"
"  for full instructions. Use the **Layouts** toolbar button to start from "
"one of pantoken's bundled\n"
"  starter page layouts (hero, callout, two-column, rubric note, "
"testimonial), sourced from\n"
"  [`@pantoken/plugin-layouts`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"plugin-layouts).\n"
"\n"
"## Develop\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"This opens a Vite dev server with:\n"
"\n"
"- An **editor** pane (TinyMCE, matching the version/config\n"
"  [instructure/canvas-lms](https://github.com/instructure/canvas-lms) itself "
"uses — see below).\n"
"  Use the **Layouts** button to load one of the bundled starter layouts "
"(this replaces the whole\n"
"  document, after a confirm, rather than inserting at the cursor), and the "
"**Source code** toggle\n"
"  to hand-edit the raw HTML in a syntax-highlighted (CodeMirror) view "
"alongside the editor, with\n"
"  the preview pane updating live as you type — unlike TinyMCE's stock `code` "
"plugin, which edits in\n"
"  a one-shot modal dialog with no live preview.\n"
"- A **preview** pane showing the editor's content with the current CSS/JS "
"tab's stylesheet/script\n"
"  applied (not just the resolved CDN URLs), wrapped to match Canvas's own "
"content-area background\n"
"  and max width — a faithful \"what this will look like once uploaded to "
"Canvas\" check, updated\n"
"  live as you type or edit the theme.\n"
"- The editor and preview panes sit in a split view you can resize by "
"dragging the divider, stack\n"
"  vertically instead of side by side, and swap the order of (drag a pane's "
"toolbar onto the other,\n"
"  or use the **Swap panes** button). Each pane has its own fullscreen "
"button.\n"
"- The **Edit theme** tray's **Config** tab holds the CDN provider/theme/mode "
"selects and\n"
"  **Download theme.css** / **Download theme.js** links; its **CSS**/**JS** "
"tabs are editable copies\n"
"  of the generated files — hand-edit them and the preview picks up your "
"changes directly. Changing\n"
"  a Config select re-generates the CSS/JS tabs unless you've already edited "
"them, in which case a\n"
"  **Regenerate from config** button appears instead of silently overwriting "
"your edit.\n"
"\n"
"## Workflow\n"
"\n"
"1. Upload `theme.css` and `theme.js` to Canvas's Theme Editor (**Advanced → "
"CSS / JavaScript**) so\n"
"   pantoken's classes are available on every page.\n"
"2. Run `npm run dev`, use **Layouts** to start from a bundled starter, and "
"edit it like you\n"
"   would in Canvas's own RCE.\n"
"3. Click **Copy HTML** and paste the result into a Canvas page's RCE (switch "
"to the HTML editor\n"
"   view first). Canvas sanitizes pasted HTML server-side — this scaffold "
"doesn't attempt to\n"
"   replicate that, so always verify the pasted result in Canvas (see \"Notes "
"on Canvas's RCE\"\n"
"   below).\n"
"\n"
"## Notes on Canvas's RCE\n"
"\n"
"The Canvas Rich Content Editor runs TinyMCE and sanitizes submitted HTML on "
"the server against an\n"
"allowlist (`gems/canvas_sanitize` in canvas-lms, kept in sync with TinyMCE's "
"own\n"
"`valid_elements`/`extended_valid_elements`). What that allowlist means for "
"templates built here:\n"
"\n"
"- `class`, `id`, `style`, `title`, `role`, and `aria-*` attributes are "
"allowed on every element —\n"
"  pantoken's `class=\"instui-*\"` styling hooks (and inline `style`, e.g. "
"for CSS anchor positioning)\n"
"  **do** survive being pasted and saved, contrary to older guidance in this "
"file. `<script>` tags\n"
"  are always stripped.\n"
"- **RCE-safe pantoken components**: static/display components — alert, view, "
"heading, text, table,\n"
"  a button-as-`<a>` (not a real `<button>`), blockquote. Stick to semantic "
"HTML pantoken already\n"
"  supports (`div`, `p`, `span`, `a`, `img`, headings, lists, tables).\n"
"- **RCE-unsafe**: anything from `@pantoken/interactions`'s behavior set — "
"modal, tooltip,\n"
"  drilldown, close-button, or any other component driven by the native "
"`popover`/`popovertarget`/\n"
"  `command`/`commandfor` attributes. Those attributes aren't in Canvas's "
"sanitizer allowlist, so\n"
"  the markup survives but the interactive behavior silently breaks the first "
"time the page is\n"
"  saved in Canvas, even with `theme.js`'s `@pantoken/interactions` loader "
"present. Real form\n"
"  elements (`input`, `form`, `button`, `select`, `textarea`, `label`) and "
"inline `<svg>` are\n"
"  stripped outright — none of the bundled starter templates use them.\n"
"\n"
"`theme.js` loads `@pantoken/interactions` from the CDN, which runs in "
"Canvas's global page scope —\n"
"useful for interactions on pages you build directly in Canvas's RCE with raw "
"HTML edits, but (per\n"
"above) any `popover`/`command`-attribute-driven markup pasted from the RCE "
"preview here won't stay\n"
"interactive once saved.\n"
msgstr ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"Opplastningsklare ressurser for Canvas LMS sin **Theme Editor**, pluss en "
"lokal forhåndsvisning for å lage Rich\n"
"Content Editor (RCE)-sidemaler stilisert med\n"
"[`@pantoken/components`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"components).\n"
"\n"
"## Hva som finnes her\n"
"\n"
"- `theme.css` / `theme.js` — last opp disse to filene under **Theme Editor → "
"Advanced** i Canvas.\n"
"  De er bygget for CDN-leverandøren/theme/mode du valgte ved scaffolding (`--"
"cdn`/`--theme`/\n"
"  `--theme-mode`; jsDelivr/rebrand/light som standard) og inkluderer en "
"loader for\n"
"  `@pantoken/interactions` (kobler opp komponentadferd som modal, tooltip og "
"drilldown).\n"
"- `index.html` / `src/main.ts` — en lokal, TinyMCE-basert editor (`npm run "
"dev`) som speiler Canvas sin\n"
"  RCE slik at du kan forfatte sidemaler mot pantoken sine klasser før du "
"kopierer dem inn i Canvas.\n"
"  Siden selv er bygget med pantoken sin `wrapper` layout: klikk **Edit "
"theme** for å åpne en skuff\n"
"  med **Config** / **CSS** / **JS** faner (CDN-leverandør/theme/mode-valg, "
"og syntaksfremhevede,\n"
"  håndredigerbare kopier av `theme.css`/`theme.js` som mater "
"forhåndsvisningen live), og **?**-knappen\n"
"  for full instruksjon. Bruk **Layouts** verktøylinjeknappen for å starte "
"fra en av pantoken sine medfølgende\n"
"  startsideoppsett (hero, callout, to-kolonner, rubric note, testimonial), "
"hentet fra\n"
"  [`@pantoken/plugin-layouts`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"plugin-layouts).\n"
"\n"
"## Utvikling\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Dette åpner en Vite dev-server med:\n"
"\n"
"- Et **editor**-panel (TinyMCE, samsvarende versjon/konfigurasjon\n"
"  [instructure/canvas-lms](https://github.com/instructure/canvas-lms) selv "
"bruker — se under).\n"
"  Bruk **Layouts**-knappen for å laste en av de medfølgende startoppsettene "
"(dette erstatter hele\n"
"  dokumentet, etter en bekreftelse, i stedet for å sette inn ved markøren), "
"og **Source code**-bryteren\n"
"  for å håndredigere rå HTML i en syntaksfremhevet (CodeMirror) visning ved "
"siden av editoren, med\n"
"  forhåndsvisningen som oppdateres live mens du skriver — i motsetning til "
"TinyMCE sin standard `code`-plugin, som redigerer i\n"
"  en engangs modal-dialog uten live forhåndsvisning.\n"
"- Et **preview**-panel som viser editorens innhold med stilarket/scriptet "
"fra den aktuelle CSS/JS-fanen\n"
"  anvendt (ikke bare de løste CDN-URLene), innpakket for å matche Canvas sin "
"egen innholdsområdes bakgrunn\n"
"  og maks bredde — en trofast \"slik vil det se ut når det er lastet opp til "
"Canvas\"-sjekk, oppdatert\n"
"  live mens du skriver eller redigerer temaet.\n"
"- Editor- og forhåndsvisningspanelene ligger i en delt visning du kan endre "
"størrelse på ved å dra skillelinjen, stable\n"
"  vertikalt i stedet for side om side, og bytte rekkefølgen på dem (dra et "
"panels verktøylinje over det andre,\n"
"  eller bruk **Swap panes**-knappen). Hvert panel har sin egen "
"fullskjermknapp.\n"
"- **Edit theme**-skuffens **Config**-fane inneholder CDN-leverandør/theme/"
"mode-valgene og\n"
"  **Download theme.css** / **Download theme.js**-lenker; dens **CSS**/**JS**-"
"faner er redigerbare kopier\n"
"  av de genererte filene — rediger dem for hånd og forhåndsvisningen plukker "
"opp endringene direkte. Å endre\n"
"  et Config-valg regenererer CSS/JS-fanene med mindre du allerede har "
"redigert dem, i så fall vises en\n"
"  **Regenerate from config**-knapp i stedet for at endringen overskriver "
"ditt arbeid stille.\n"
"\n"
"## Arbeidsflyt\n"
"\n"
"1. Last opp `theme.css` og `theme.js` til Canvas sin Theme Editor "
"(**Advanced → CSS / JavaScript**) slik at\n"
"   pantoken sine klasser er tilgjengelige på hver side.\n"
"2. Kjør `npm run dev`, bruk **Layouts** for å starte fra en medfølgende "
"starter, og rediger det som du\n"
"   ville gjort i Canvas sin egen RCE.\n"
"3. Klikk **Copy HTML** og lim resultatet inn i en Canvas-sides RCE (bytt "
"først til HTML-editor\n"
"   visningen). Canvas saniterer limt HTML på serversiden — dette scaffold "
"forsøker ikke å\n"
"   replikere det, så verifiser alltid det limte resultatet i Canvas (se "
"\"Merk om Canvas sin RCE\"\n"
"   nedenfor).\n"
"\n"
"## Merknader om Canvas sin RCE\n"
"\n"
"Canvas Rich Content Editor kjører TinyMCE og saniterer innsendt HTML på "
"serveren mot en\n"
"allowlist (`gems/canvas_sanitize` i canvas-lms, holdt i synk med TinyMCE sin "
"egen\n"
"`valid_elements`/`extended_valid_elements`). Hva den allowlisten betyr for "
"maler bygget her:\n"
"\n"
"- `class`, `id`, `style`, `title`, `role`, og `aria-*` attributter er "
"tillatt på hvert element —\n"
"  pantoken sine `class=\"instui-*\"` styling-kroker (og inline `style`, "
"f.eks. for CSS-forankringsposisjonering)\n"
"  **overlever** å bli limt inn og lagret, i motsetning til eldre råd i denne "
"filen. `<script>`-tagger\n"
"  blir alltid fjernet.\n"
"- **RCE-sikre pantoken-komponenter**: statiske/visningskomponenter — alert, "
"view, heading, text, table,\n"
"  en knapp-som-`<a>` (ikke en ekte `<button>`), blockquote. Hold deg til "
"semantisk HTML pantoken allerede\n"
"  støtter (`div`, `p`, `span`, `a`, `img`, overskrifter, lister, tabeller).\n"
"- **RCE-usikre**: alt fra `@pantoken/interactions`'s adferdssett — modal, "
"tooltip,\n"
"  drilldown, close-button, eller enhver annen komponent drevet av native "
"`popover`/`popovertarget`/\n"
"  `command`/`commandfor` attributter. Disse attributtene er ikke i Canvas "
"sin sanitizer-allowlist, så\n"
"  markupen overlever men den interaktive adferden brytes stille første gang "
"siden lagres i Canvas, selv med `theme.js` sin `@pantoken/interactions` "
"loader til stede. Ekte skjemaelementer (`input`, `form`, `button`, `select`, "
"`textarea`, `label`) og inline `<svg>` blir\n"
"  fjernet helt — ingen av de medfølgende startmalene bruker dem.\n"
"\n"
"`theme.js` laster `@pantoken/interactions` fra CDN-en, som kjører i Canvas "
"sin globale sidescope —\n"
"nyttig for interaksjoner på sider du bygger direkte i Canvas sin RCE med rå "
"HTML-redigering, men (som nevnt\n"
"ovenfor) vil enhver `popover`/`command`-attributt-drevet markup limt fra RCE-"
"forhåndsvisningen her ikke forbli\n"
"interaktiv når den er lagret.\n"

#: components/README.md
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"A plain TypeScript app (via Vite) styled with\n"
"[`@pantoken/components`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"components), Instructure's\n"
"design tokens and icons.\n"
"\n"
"## Develop\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## What's here\n"
"\n"
"- `index.html` holds the actual page markup — a `wrapper`-layout shell from\n"
"  [`@pantoken/plugin-layouts`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"plugin-layouts). View source\n"
"  and edit it directly; nothing is injected by JavaScript.\n"
"- `src/main.ts` imports `@pantoken/css` (defines every `--instui-*` custom "
"property),\n"
"  `@pantoken/components/base.css` (document defaults + focus ring), "
"`components.css`\n"
"  (`.instui-*` classes), `@pantoken/interactions` (wires up modal, tooltip, "
"and other component\n"
"  behaviors out of the box), and your own `src/style.css` — add interactive "
"behavior here.\n"
"- Optional insertion points (header, filters, content, trailing) are marked "
"with\n"
"  `<div data-slot=\"...\">` in `index.html` — replace their contents with "
"your own markup.\n"
"- Apply classes like `class=\"instui-button\"` to markup; see the\n"
"  [component reference](https://pantoken.app/api/css) for the full class "
"list.\n"
"\n"
"## Learn more\n"
"\n"
"See the [HTML guide](https://pantoken.app/guide/components) to learn more.\n"
msgstr ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"En enkel TypeScript-app (via Vite) stylet med\n"
"[`@pantoken/components`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"components), Instructures\n"
"design tokens og ikoner.\n"
"\n"
"## Utvikling\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Hva som finnes her\n"
"\n"
"- `index.html` inneholder den faktiske sidens markup — et `wrapper`-layout-"
"skall fra\n"
"  [`@pantoken/plugin-layouts`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"plugin-layouts). Se kilden\n"
"  og rediger den direkte; ingenting injiseres av JavaScript.\n"
"- `src/main.ts` importerer `@pantoken/css` (definerer alle `--instui-*` "
"egendefinerte\n"
"  properties), `@pantoken/components/base.css` (dokumentstandarder + focus "
"ring), `components.css`\n"
"  (`.instui-*` klasser), `@pantoken/interactions` (kobler opp modal, tooltip "
"og andre\n"
"  komponentoppførsel rett ut av boksen), og din egen `src/style.css` — legg "
"til interaktiv\n"
"  oppførsel her.\n"
"- Valgfrie innssettingspunkter (header, filters, content, trailing) er "
"markert med\n"
"  `<div data-slot=\"...\">` i `index.html` — erstatt innholdet deres med din "
"egen markup.\n"
"- Bruk klasser som `class=\"instui-button\"` på markup; se\n"
"  [komponentreferansen](https://pantoken.app/api/css) for fullstendig liste "
"over klasser.\n"
"\n"
"## Lær mer\n"
"\n"
"Se [HTML-guiden](https://pantoken.app/guide/components) for mer "
"informasjon.\n"

#: next/README.md
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"A Next.js (App Router) app styled with [`@pantoken/next`](https://"
"www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/next),\n"
"Instructure's design tokens and icons.\n"
"\n"
"## Develop\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## What's here\n"
"\n"
"- `next.config.mjs` wraps the config with `withPantoken(...)` (adds pantoken "
"to\n"
"  `transpilePackages`).\n"
"- `app/layout.tsx` imports `@pantoken/css`, which defines every `--instui-*` "
"custom\n"
"  property, at the root so it's available on every page, plus the `wrapper` "
"layout's root class on\n"
"  `<body>` and `PantokenInteractions` (a client component that loads "
"`@pantoken/interactions` —\n"
"  wires up modal, tooltip, and other component behaviors out of the box).\n"
"- `app/page.tsx` renders markup styled with `instui-*` classes; optional "
"insertion points (header,\n"
"  filters, content, trailing) are marked with `<div data-slot=\"...\">`.\n"
"\n"
"## Learn more\n"
"\n"
"See the [getting started guide](https://pantoken.app/guide/getting-started) "
"to learn more.\n"
msgstr ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"En Next.js (App Router) app stylet med [`@pantoken/next`](https://"
"www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/next), Instructures designtokener og "
"ikoner.\n"
"\n"
"## Utvikling\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Hva som finnes her\n"
"\n"
"- `next.config.mjs` pakker inn konfigurasjonen med `withPantoken(...)` "
"(legger til pantoken i `transpilePackages`).\n"
"- `app/layout.tsx` importerer `@pantoken/css`, som definerer alle `--instui-"
"*` egendefinerte\n"
"  egenskaper, i roten slik at de er tilgjengelige på hver side, pluss "
"`wrapper` layoutens rotklasse på\n"
"  `<body>` og `PantokenInteractions` (en klientkomponent som laster "
"`@pantoken/interactions` —\n"
"  kobler opp modal, tooltip og andre komponentoppførsel umiddelbart).\n"
"- `app/page.tsx` rendererer markup stylet med `instui-*` klasser; valgfrie "
"innsettingspunkter (header,\n"
